simple patterns (vocab=256, len=1024, n=200/pattern):
  uniform baseline ln(V) = 5.5452 nats   (an unstructured iid sequence is irreducible at this value)

  pattern                 pad%   floor  unigram  gzip  floor/lnV
  --------------------------------------------------------------
  periodic                  0%  0.0219   5.3322  0.03      0.004
  palindrome                0%  2.7726   5.5401  1.02      0.500
  copy                      0%  2.3153   5.5413  0.47      0.418
  reverse                   0%  2.7753   5.5424  1.02      0.500
  counting_anbn             0%  0.1751   5.1907  0.12      0.032
  counting_anbncn           0%  0.1263   5.2970  0.13      0.023
  nested                    0%  2.7726   5.5401  1.02      0.500
  interleaving              0%  0.0108   5.1394  0.03      0.002
  permutation_cycle         0%  0.0189   5.2989  0.04      0.003
  hierarchical              0%  0.0163   5.2459  0.04      0.003
  noisy_palindrome*         0%  3.2735   5.5402  1.02      0.590
  random                    0%  5.5452   5.5407  1.02      1.000
  identity                  0%  0.0054   4.7662  0.03      0.001
  composite_mirror_repeat    0%  1.3863   5.5389  0.55      0.250
  mixer*                    1%  1.3801   5.5280  0.53      0.249  <- PAD INSIDE BODY!

  Legend:
    pad%      : fraction of tokens that are the reserved masked pad (ID 0; excluded from the loss)
    floor     : min achievable mean loss over UNMASKED tokens (the true training floor)
    unigram   : naive global-unigram cross-entropy (memorization baseline)
    gzip      : mean gzip compression ratio (README complexity metric)
    floor/lnV : floor as a fraction of the uniform baseline (0 = fully predictable, 1 = unstructured)
    *         : floor is a LOOSE lower bound (true floor is higher); counting_* use a dedicated EXACT oracle

